# Wave W17-X (Route 209): bell sand — tower-road pale sand, design-authorised: a pale grey-cream sand running Inglenook’s domes to Repose under the tower’s bell, kept quiet and cool so the tower plot’s drifts read as the colour on the road (design: the quiet pilgrim path running past the still tower). Split from Route 210’s warmer ranch sand by the coolness entire — bell light vs pasture light — and from Route 201’s shore sand by the grey: this sand is trodden by pilgrims, not blown off a lake.
